 "text": "My desk was once covered in papers, cups and cables. I told myself that I knew where everything was. In truth, I lost time searching for things every day. So I made a few rules. At the end of each day, I clear the desk completely. Papers go into one tray, and anything I do not need goes in the bin. Cables are tied together and kept out of sight. In the morning, I start with an empty surface. It sounds like a small change, but it helps me begin work quickly and calmly. A tidy space at the start of the day makes it easier to think clearly."
